From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sqm-hotplug: on ifdown, stop the queues whose device is gone

netifd sets DEVICE only for ifup and ifupdate, so the hotplug's check for
it ended every ifdown before its stop: an ifdown never stopped anything. A
queue on a device that goes with its interface (pppoe-wan, a tunnel) kept
its ifb, with its CAKE, and its state file until the next ifup, or for
good if the interface stayed down.

On ifdown the hotplug stops each running queue whose device no longer
exists. A queue on a device that's still there keeps running, as it did:
the ifdown can be another interface's on the same device (wan6 on wan's
eth1), and qdiscs stay on a device that goes down. If the device is still
there at the ifdown and goes after, the next ifup's reload finds its
qdiscs gone and starts it again.

diff --git a/platform/openwrt/sqm-hotplug b/platform/openwrt/sqm-hotplug
index 5b35071..8aa0084 100755
--- a/platform/openwrt/sqm-hotplug
+++ b/platform/openwrt/sqm-hotplug
@@ -2,6 +2,20 @@
 
 . /lib/functions.sh
 
+# netifd names no device on ifdown. A queue whose device went with the
+# interface (pppoe-wan, a tunnel) is stopped, so its ifb and state file
+# don't stay behind; one on a device that's still there (eth1, which wan6
+# shares with wan) keeps running.
+if [ "$ACTION" = ifdown ]; then
+    . /etc/sqm/sqm.conf
+    for f in ${SQM_STATE_DIR}/*.state; do
+        dev=${f##*/}
+        dev=${dev%.state}
+        [ -f "$f" ] && [ ! -d "/sys/class/net/$dev" ] && /usr/lib/sqm/run.sh stop "$dev"
+    done
+    exit 0
+fi
+
 [ -n "$DEVICE" ] || exit 0
 
 list_ports() {
@@ -34,9 +48,3 @@ reload_sqm() {
 }
 
 [ "$ACTION" = ifup ] && /etc/init.d/sqm enabled && reload_sqm
-
-if [ "$ACTION" = ifdown ]; then
-    for dev in $ALL_DEVICES; do
-        /usr/lib/sqm/run.sh stop $dev
-    done
-fi
